---
import { site } from "../../data/site";
---

<section class="section faq" id="faq">
    <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-rail">
            <p class="kicker">Sec. 05 / Troubleshooting</p>
            <p class="fig-label">FIG. 07 — Q &amp; A</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sec-body">
            <h2>The fine print.</h2>
            <p class="lead">
                The store, the hardware, the permissions, the network —
                the answers we give most often, in full,{" "}
                <em>license terms included.</em>
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <details>
        <summary>Is it on the Play Store?</summary>
        <p>
            Not yet. The alpha ships as a signed APK you install
            yourself. The full build can drive other apps through
            Android accessibility, which Play restricts — a reduced
            build is planned for stores, while the full one stays
            sideloaded.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Do I need a computer?</summary>
        <p>
            No. Setup, the agent, the terminal and the model keys
            all live on the phone.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Which phones does it run on?</summary>
        <p>
            Arm64 devices on Android {site.minAndroid} or newer,
            with 2 GB free. It will not run on x86 emulators or
            32-bit phones.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>What can it actually control?</summary>
        <p>
            Any app with a visible UI: tapping, typing, scrolling,
            reading the screen, plus notifications, clipboard,
            sharing and intents. Actions that change the phone need
            a biometric unlock first.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Does it need a constant connection?</summary>
        <p>
            The agent and your files run locally. Model calls go to
            the provider you configure, so it needs network for
            those — unless you point it at a local endpoint.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Can I use the source?</summary>
        <p>
            The source is on{" "}
            <a href={site.repo} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                GitHub
            </a>{" "}
            under a source-available license. You can read it and
            contribute; you cannot copy, use, or redistribute it.
            The official app is the only distributed build.
        </p>
    </details>
</section>
